{number: 14}
{title: How Great Thou Art}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C] Lord, my God! When I in [F] awesome wonder
Con-[C] sider all the [G] worlds Thy hands have [C] made,
I [C] see the stars, I hear the [F] rolling thunder,
Thy [C] power through-[G] out the universe dis-[C] played.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Then sings my [C] soul, my [F] Savior God, to [C] Thee:
How great Thou [Dm] art, [G7] how great Thou [C] art! [G]
Then sings my [C] soul, my [F] Savior God, to [C] Thee:
How great Thou [Dm] art, [G7] how great Thou [C] art!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] through the woods and forest [F] glades I wander,
And [C] hear the birds sing [G] sweetly in the [C] trees;
When [C] I look down from lofty [F] mountain grandeur,
And [C] hear the brook and [G] feel the gentle [C] breeze.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C] when I think that God, His [F] Son not sparing,
Sent [C] Him to die, I [G] scarce can take it [C] in;
That [C] on the cross, my burden [F] gladly bearing,
He [C] bled and died to [G] take away my [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [C] Christ shall come, with shout of [F] acclamation,
And [C] take me home, what [G] joy shall fill my [C] heart!
Then [C] I shall bow in humble [F] adoration,
And [C] there proclaim, my [G] God, how great Thou [C] art!
{end_of_verse}
